        "eyebrow": "Virtual staging & 3D rendering · Dallas–Fort Worth",
        "heading": "Virtual Staging for Home Builders: Dallas–Fort Worth",
        "lede": "Virtual staging is a digital marketing technique for real estate — the process of adding furniture and decor to listing photos: an interior designer furnishes empty or cleared rooms in the image so buyers can judge scale and layout, without any physical furniture entering the house. Bella's designers stage new construction, spec homes and model-plan builds for DFW home builders — and listings for agents — in 24 to 48 hours, from {price:virtual-staging} a photo, and render homes that aren't built yet from your plans.",
        "cta_label": "Stage my listing — from {price:virtual-staging}",
        "cta_link": "/products/virtual-staging",
        "alt_label": "3D renderings for builders",
        "alt_link": "/products/3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization",
        "city": "Dallas",
        "market_heading": "Why virtual staging matters for Dallas–Fort Worth home builders",
        "market_text": "<p>Dallas–Fort Worth adds more people each year than almost any metro in the country, and a large share of them are relocating on a corporate timeline from California, Illinois or the Northeast. They build a shortlist online weeks before they fly in, and an empty room gives them nothing to judge but square footage.</p><p>The other half of the market is new construction. Builders across Plano, Frisco, McKinney, Prosper and Celina list spec homes and model-plan builds where several homes in a community share the same floor plans. Photographed empty, they're indistinguishable — new construction staging is what makes one of them the listing a relocating buyer remembers.</p><p>Virtual staging also takes furniture logistics off the job site. There's no furniture to move through an active community, no rental contract per home and no rental clock if a spec home sits: staging is {price:virtual-staging} a photo, once. Designers can show one floor plan in several styles for different buyers, and a bonus room as an office, game room or nursery.</p><p>Before a home is built, there is nothing to photograph. Bella's <a href=\"/products/3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization\">3D rendering service</a> turns your plans into photorealistic exteriors and interiors from {price:3d-rendering} an image — 3D rendering for home builders, Dallas to Fort Worth — so you can pre-sell from plans and launch community pages before construction is complete. The <a href=\"/pages/home-builder-marketing\">home builder marketing guide</a> covers the full pre-sale playbook, and our <a href=\"/pages/virtual-staging-texas\">virtual staging in Texas</a> page covers Houston, Austin and San Antonio.</p><p>97% of buyers use the internet in their home search (NAR), so the listing photos are where most buyers first compare homes, and in NAR's 2025 Profile of Home Staging, 83% of buyers' agents said staging made it easier for a buyer to visualize the property as a future home. Virtually staged photos show what each room is for and how much furniture it really holds, so the house makes the shortlist before anyone books a showing.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Virtual staging Dallas builders and agents can list the same week",
        "local_text": "<p>Designers stage modern-transitional for Plano, Frisco and McKinney new builds, warmer traditional for Highland Park and Lakewood, and clean contemporary for Uptown and Design District condos.</p><p>Builder inventory is quoted as a batch and delivered together, so a whole community's worth of listings lands at once rather than photo by photo. Files come back NTREIS-ready with disclosure guidance included: label each virtually staged photo, note it in the agent remarks and keep the original photo available.</p><p>Virtual staging, DFW-wide, happens online: there's no walkthrough to schedule anywhere in the Metroplex or across Texas. Order, upload your photos and a designer handles the styling. Volume discounts apply automatically — 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+ — which is where most builder sets land. Modern and transitional styles suit most DFW new construction, while Lakewood Tudors and Craftsman bungalows get warmer traditional pieces in wood tones.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we stage most",
        "hoods": "Plano, Frisco, McKinney, Prosper, Celina, Allen, Uptown, Highland Park, Lakewood, Arlington, Fort Worth",
        "cred_text": "From {price:virtual-staging} a photo · 3D renders from {price:3d-rendering} · 24–48 hour staging · Real designers, never AI"
      }
